WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.440
From cowboy shootouts to shocking scenes&nbsp;
at a Native American residential school,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:09.120
Taylor Sheridan's 1923 takes viewers&nbsp;
from rural Montana to Africa and beyond.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.000
Here's a behind the scenes look at&nbsp;
the latest Yellowstone spin-off.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:17.040
Though the flagship Yellowstone series has been&nbsp;
on the air for five seasons, each more intense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:22.680
than the last, not every spin-off has received&nbsp;
a second round. 1883 was a one-and-done limited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:27.300
series that creator Taylor Sheridan himself&nbsp;
described as a, quote, "10-hour movie with an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:32.340
ending." Rather than simply continuing the&nbsp;
story, 1923 skips forward four decades to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:36.660
witness the now-established Duttons fight for&nbsp;
survival during Montana's Great Depression.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:40.920
But unlike its predecessor, 1923 earned a&nbsp;
second season with the promise to continue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:45.120
the exhilarating story of Jacob and Cara&nbsp;
Dutton into another year. While this isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.540
the first Paramount-Sheridan co-production&nbsp;
to find itself with more stories to tell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:51.660
it is the first Yellowstone spin-off&nbsp;
to earn a direct continuation.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.940
When talking with Deadline about the renewal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:57.060
Sheridan revealed that the second season&nbsp;
would also consist of eight episodes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:01.440
Explaining why the 1883 follow-up would&nbsp;
be more than a single season, he said,

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.200
"I need to do this in two blocks. An eight-episode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.960
block and a second eight-episode&nbsp;
block to wrap this up. [...] For&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:10.560
[Paramount], it is great because they get&nbsp;
more content. For me, I get more runway."

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.620
One thing's for sure, we can't&nbsp;
complain about more Dutton adventures.

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:18.960
When Sheridan first announced his new wave&nbsp;
of Yellowstone spin-offs, 1923 was originally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:23.280
billed as a different series altogether. Wanting&nbsp;
to tell the story of Montana's Great Depression,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:27.360
which began before the economic catastrophe&nbsp;
hit the rest of America in the 1930s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:33.000
Sheridan had initially titled the series 1932. But&nbsp;
a deeper dive into Montana's history changed that.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.800
By the time the series entered production, the&nbsp;
last two digits in the title had swapped. Rather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:41.940
than chronicling the nationwide Great Depression,&nbsp;
the series tackles the fallout of World War I,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:47.040
the 1920s Prohibition era, and Montana's own&nbsp;
Depression, which started nearly a decade earlier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:51.300
and involved a host of cattle and range wars.&nbsp;
While the premise of a Great Depression-era tale&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:56.400
is interesting in and of itself, 1923 is unique&nbsp;
in that it can cover multiple eras of American&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:00.660
and world history at once all while invoking&nbsp;
the works of John Steinbeck in the process.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:05.400
No doubt, the change served the series well in&nbsp;
the long run, allowing for it to include Spencer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:09.780
Dutton's post-War voyage to Africa as a hired&nbsp;
gun. This has been one of the more impressive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:14.400
storylines on the series and has stretched the&nbsp;
Yellowstone franchise into international waters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.700
In addition, the commentary on&nbsp;
the impulsiveness of the 1920s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:21.540
mixed with the desperation of a depression&nbsp;
makes for some instantly dramatic content.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:26.820
"He survived the night. That's a start."

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:31.620
It's no secret that the years 1923 and&nbsp;
1883 are more than a couple decades&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:35.820
apart. Since most of the 1883 cast is&nbsp;
killed off by the limited series' end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:40.200
that leaves very few options for the Dutton family&nbsp;
to continue their bloodline. Because of this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:44.520
James Dutton's older brother Jacob and his wife&nbsp;
Cara take over the Dutton homestead and carry on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:48.960
the family legacy in 1923. Though Harrison&nbsp;
Ford and Helen Mirren headline the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:52.020
there are two others who bridge the gap&nbsp;
from the first prequel and this one.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:57.120
For starters, the series is narrated by actress&nbsp;
Isabel May, who played Elsa Dutton — the firstborn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:03.120
daughter of James and Margaret, on 1883. Though&nbsp;
Elsa dies in 1883, her spirit still haunts her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:07.740
family's land, and intends to watch over the&nbsp;
Dutton legacy from afar. May herself is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:12.540
only cast member from 1883 to lend her talents&nbsp;
to Sheridan's latest prequel, vocal or otherwise.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:16.860
Of course, a young John Dutton Sr. was&nbsp;
present during the events of 1883 as well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:19.440
played then by Audie Rick.&nbsp;
Though Rick doesn't return,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:24.960
John Sr. is the only character from 1883 to&nbsp;
physically return in 1923, though not for long.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:30.180
While most actors prefer to see a script&nbsp;
before signing onto a commitment like 1923,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:35.460
neither Harrison Ford nor Helen Mirren did so.&nbsp;
Though he'd planned all of 1883 out beforehand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:39.060
Taylor Sheridan had only a rough&nbsp;
idea of where he wanted 1923 to go,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:43.506
though he knew exactly who he wanted&nbsp;
to cast. He told Deadline in 2022,

00:03:43.506 --> 00:03:46.560
"I need to know who I'm writing for.&nbsp;
I'm done wondering who I'm writing for,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:49.380
and I have to go try to chase the&nbsp;
person I had in my mind and I can't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:51.540
get the person because they're&nbsp;
doing some [other] Netflix show."

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:55.620
This wasn't so with Ford and Mirren. In&nbsp;
that same interview, Sheridan explained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:58.740
that Ford flew himself down to Texas to&nbsp;
meet with him at his own private ranch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:01.320
and he talked the movie star&nbsp;
into it over a bottle of wine.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:03.420
"I have what my family fought for."

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:05.400
Sheridan went on,

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:08.340
"Then came Helen [Mirren], and&nbsp;
same thing. Have a glass of wine."

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:10.560
Sheridan has quite a reputation in Hollywood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:13.380
one that flocks big names&nbsp;
towards the Yellowstone universe.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:16.440
In an interview with The Hollywood&nbsp;
Reporter, Ford explained why he took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:20.520
roles on both Shrinking on Apple TV+&nbsp;
and Sheridan's latest prequel, saying,

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:23.700
"I took the job without a script&nbsp;
on both of them, on faith that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.520
people who created the projects were&nbsp;
going to deliver me a good script."

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:32.220
Would you believe that 1923 is one of the most&nbsp;
expensive television projects ever? With Harrison&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:36.540
Ford and Helen Mirren on board, not to mention the&nbsp;
immaculate set design and production value that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:40.980
tosses us backwards a century, there's no denying&nbsp;
that the latest Taylor Sheridan Yellowstone series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:45.840
is putting its money where its mouth is. In fact,&nbsp;
Sheridan told Deadline that he believes 1883 was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:51.420
the most expensive first season ever made, only&nbsp;
for 1923 to exceed that. Sheridan told Deadline,

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:53.580
"I don't know what the Game&nbsp;
of Thrones budgets were,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:55.500
but I don't know how they could&nbsp;
have been more than this."

00:04:55.905 --> 00:05:00.945
"You're going to hang us? Hey? Hang me!"

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.360
In the same interview, the&nbsp;
filmmaker estimates they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:06.120
spending around $22 million per episode, saying,

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:09.840
"I didn't do very good in math in school.&nbsp;
But I can multiply eight and three and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:13.260
add a bunch of zeros and realize I&nbsp;
just asked for 150 million dollars."

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:17.580
No doubt, Game of Thrones averaged $15&nbsp;
million per episode by its final season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:20.820
meaning that the budget for&nbsp;
1923 quickly surpassed it.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:24.600
When compared to the flagship series,&nbsp;
1923 cost more than the first three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:28.980
seasons of the Kevin Costner-led production&nbsp;
combined. According to The Salt Lake Tribune,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:33.360
Yellowstone spent somewhere around $80 million&nbsp;
in Utah during the series' first few years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:37.140
back when they used to film there rather&nbsp;
than in Montana. With the show's success,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:42.120
that budget has no doubt gotten larger, but&nbsp;
certainly not as large as $150 million total.

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:47.280
Though the Yellowstone saga is most well-known&nbsp;
for shooting primarily in Montana — a change&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:52.140
the franchise made after a few years of filming&nbsp;
in northern Utah — not every plotline in 1923&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:56.820
revolves around the Dutton family ranch. Though&nbsp;
the flagship series primarily shoots in Missoula,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.820 --> 00:06:00.540
Montana, 1923's time in Montana&nbsp;
was mostly centered in Butte.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:05.580
A historic mining town, Butte lies about halfway&nbsp;
between Bozeman and Missoula and gives off a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:10.500
turn-of-the-century vibe that lends itself well&nbsp;
to the 1920s time period. But not every 1923&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:15.000
character resides in Montana. As Spencer Dutton&nbsp;
spends the majority of the series away from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:19.440
family homestead, his adventures with Alex take&nbsp;
him across Africa and into international waters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:23.820
in hopes of reaching the United States. But these&nbsp;
scenes weren't shot in some Hollywood studio.

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:26.880
"Darling there are not words to describe&nbsp;
the pickle we just found ourselves in."

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:31.020
"Is it bad?" "We need a higher tree."

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:35.400
Unlike the other Yellowstone series,&nbsp;
which exclusively film within the U.S.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:40.140
1923 branched out with on-location shooting&nbsp;
in Africa. The show's first season made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:43.620
its way into a few different countries&nbsp;
across the globe, including South Africa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:47.280
Kenya, Tanzania, and Malta, which is&nbsp;
considered part of Southern Europe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:51.120
The production even stopped briefly&nbsp;
in Kabul, the capital of Afghanistan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:56.700
which is technically part of Asia. Including North&nbsp;
America, that's four continents touched by 1923.

00:06:57.420 --> 00:07:00.780
Ever since Yellowstone became the&nbsp;
Paramount Network's breakout hit series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:04.560
the long-running Hollywood studio has given&nbsp;
Taylor Sheridan free reign when it comes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:08.760
the Yellowstone universe and beyond. Launching&nbsp;
four different series since the flagship series'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:13.500
success, Sheridan has built quite the catalog of&nbsp;
Paramount-produced content that only seems to keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:18.060
growing. Between the Yellowstone spin-offs and his&nbsp;
other unrelated stories, Sheridan's got it made.

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:22.920
When the first episode of 1923 debuted on&nbsp;
Paramount+, it instantly broke every record&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:28.260
as the streamer's biggest series debut. After&nbsp;
1923 garnered upwards of 7 million viewers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:33.240
Paramount Media Networks' CEO Chris McCarthy&nbsp;
deemed it the #1 new cable premiere of the year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:38.700
making the second season a sure-fire thing. As&nbsp;
the story of the 1920s band of Duttons continues,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:42.360
the intrigue and mystery surrounding Donald&nbsp;
Whitfield's land-grabbing plot grows,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:46.200
and will no doubt continue to bring&nbsp;
more viewers in. David C. Glasser,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:48.660
101 Studio's CEO, said of the screenwriting,

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:52.620
"[Sheridan's] scripts attract not only the best&nbsp;
actors working today but the best crew around.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:56.760
[...] We are so fortunate these huge audiences&nbsp;
tune in to be a part of his universe every week."

00:07:57.300 --> 00:07:58.920
Between the globe-trotting spectacle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:03.180
the gorgeous cinematography, and the powerful&nbsp;
performances by Harrison Ford, Helen Mirren,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:07.140
and the rest of the phenomenal cast, it's&nbsp;
obvious why audiences continue to show up.

00:08:07.140 --> 00:08:10.680
"Grab ahold of this. Catch your breath."
 
 &nbsp;

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:15.600
When 1923 first aired, there was a lot of initial&nbsp;
confusion as to who the characters are and where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:19.680
they land on the Dutton family tree. To set the&nbsp;
record straight, Harrison Ford's Jacob Dutton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:24.960
is the older brother of Tim McGraw's James, the&nbsp;
family patriarch from 1883. Though Jacob and his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:28.980
wife Cara don't have children, they've come to&nbsp;
see James' sons John and Spencer as their own.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:34.020
While John dies early on, his son Jack continues&nbsp;
on the Dutton name and legacy with his wife Liz.

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:39.240
Fans of 1883 and 1923 might've been a bit confused&nbsp;
by the addition of Spencer Dutton, who doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:44.220
appear at all on the former series since he hasn't&nbsp;
been born yet. But flashbacks to the year 1893 —&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:48.840
as seen during Yellowstone Season 4 — reveal that&nbsp;
Spencer was born sometime after the death of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:52.680
older sister Elsa. Though there's some debate&nbsp;
as to whether Spencer or Jack will father John&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:57.660
Dutton II, it's possible that Jack is actually a&nbsp;
younger John himself, though only time will tell.

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:02.100
There's no doubt that the works of Taylor&nbsp;
Sheridan are highly praised by audiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:07.560
across the country, but his content isn't exactly&nbsp;
for the faint of heart. His 2017 movie Wind River&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:11.280
features a horrific rape scene that highlights&nbsp;
the plight of many Native American women,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:15.840
and many episodes of Yellowstone have shed light&nbsp;
on the same. Though nothing can prepare audiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:20.760
for the brutality of the Indian boarding school&nbsp;
scenes in 1923, which really push the envelope.

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:27.000
"Okay, okay, okay, okay, okay, okay."

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:30.210
"Okay what?"

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:33.960
Prior to shooting, actor Sebastian&nbsp;
Roché, the man behind Father Renaud,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:38.040
reportedly apologized to his Indigenous&nbsp;
castmates, not wishing to sugarcoat this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:42.060
dark chapter in North American history. When&nbsp;
talking with TV Insider, Roché explained,

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:46.620
"In 1923, those residential schools were a&nbsp;
blight on our history. I think it's a very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:50.040
important subject matter to talk about, because&nbsp;
it's something that we really don't know about."

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:53.160
Roché said he believes that,&nbsp;
as storytellers, their goal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:56.940
shouldn't just be entertaining audiences,&nbsp;
but challenging them with the truth, adding,

00:09:56.940 --> 00:10:00.300
"I felt a responsibility as an&nbsp;
actor to be as truthful as I could."

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:04.800
It's true that the residential schools&nbsp;
were horrific, and as recently as May 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:08.520
the United States alone has found 53&nbsp;
different burial sights associated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:12.600
with them. Now is certainly the time to shed&nbsp;
some light on this horrific period in history.

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:18.600
Many of the cast members of 1923 were forced&nbsp;
to endure Taylor Sheridan's cowboy boot camp&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:22.380
to prepare them for the harsh conditions&nbsp;
of Montana ranch life. Sheridan has a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:26.520
history of making his worlds feel authentic by&nbsp;
hiring real-life cowboys like Forrie J. Smith&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:31.140
as members of the Yellowstone cast. Brian&nbsp;
Geraghty, who plays Dutton ranch hand Zane,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.140 --> 00:10:34.800
revealed to E! News that Sheridan's boot&nbsp;
camp wasn't exactly a walk in the park.

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:40.200
"And so we were running on horses, lassoing,&nbsp;
learned how to use an old six shooter."

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:45.780
But one cast member wasn't forced to endure the&nbsp;
rigorous training prior to production. Harrison&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:50.280
Ford got out of it, but only because he's a ranch&nbsp;
owner himself. He told The Hollywood Reporter,

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:54.600
"I've owned horses for 40 years. I lived&nbsp;
in Wyoming for 40 years. I'm still living&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:57.660
there part-time. It's just getting&nbsp;
back in contact with horses, really."

00:10:57.660 --> 00:11:02.340
According to The Land Report, Ford's owned&nbsp;
his Jackson-based ranch since the 1980s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:06.180
which is all the necessary qualifications&nbsp;
he needs to play a Dutton. If anyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:08.580
knows what it means to preserve&nbsp;
what's yours, it would be Ford,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:12.360
who keeps both his treasured land and his&nbsp;
personal life pretty close to the chest.
 

